    "comment": "yellow box fade in -- ROUND 18 (r18-misc), retimed to the cabinet's own change_courseselect. enso_normal/song_select/song_select_main_genre.nulm sprite #29 label change_courseselect = f45; kanban (the whole panel wheel) alpha 1->0 LINEAR over f45..f59 (233 ms), a 10-frame dead beat f59..f69 (167 ms), then course_select (backboard + cards) and option alpha 0->1 LINEAR over f69..f98 (483 ms). Total 54 f = 900 ms @60fps. Was duration 200 with delay 16.duration+13.duration = 500: the dead beat was 100 ms too long and the fade itself 283 ms too fast, so the board popped in instead of fading. Measured with lumen_anim_dump.exe --sprite 29 --all --range 45,98; full per-frame table in Graphics/song_select/MAPPING.md ROUND 18. Not routed through anim_export.py because the curve is consumed by the ENGINE's FadeAnimation, not by the Lua sampler -- two linear segments need no table."
